%%label IV. Allegro non troppo
%%note A minor, ending in A major. A march grown from the first movement's theme, in the brass over hammering strings; a second strain; the first movement's flute melody recalled by cellos and horn; a short fugato; the march again; a slower coda in which the brass turn the theme to the major while the rest of the orchestra repeats one note.
X:1
T:Shostakovich’s Missing Symphony
T:IV. Allegro non troppo
C:Lor, in the manner of Shostakovich
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:"Allegro non troppo" 1/4=126
%%score [fl ob cl bn] [hn tp tb] tm xy [v1 v2 va vc cb]
% The score is written at sounding pitch. Dynamics in the wind, brass and double-bass parts are set one to three levels below the strings to balance the playback samples of this site; they are a playback compromise, not dynamics for live players.
